+# Spec: JSON Merge Patch
+
+Standard: JSON Merge Patch, RFC 7396 §2 (the request cites RFC 7386, which RFC 7396 obsoletes with the same
+algorithm; the constitution also names 7396). Pointer/Patch features are unaffected.
+
+## Request
+Export `applyMergePatch(target, patch)` from `src/index.ts`; returns the merged document.
+
+## Requirements
+- FR-1: If `patch` is not an object (array, string, number, boolean, `null`), the result is a copy of `patch` (§2).
+- FR-2: Otherwise, a non-object target is treated as `{}`; each patch member whose value is `null` removes that
+  member from the result; any other value is merged recursively (§2 `MergePatch`). Arrays are replaced whole.
+- FR-3: Inputs are never mutated; result shares no structure with them. `__proto__`/`constructor`/`prototype`
+  keys are plain data members and never touch prototypes.
+- FR-4: Documented with a doc comment and README entry. No errors are defined by the RFC, so none are thrown.
+
+## Edge cases
+Null patch → `null`; `{"a":{"b":null}}` onto a missing `a` gives `{"a":{}}`; non-object target with object patch
+drops nulls; array in patch replaces array in target.
